# The two-body problem, which is the only gravitational system anyone can solve
# exactly, and so the project's primary validation instrument.
#
# An eccentric orbit released at periapsis, integrated for two hundred
# revolutions at two hundred steps each. No softening: a Kepler orbit is an orbit
# of two point masses, and softening it would replace the problem whose solution
# is known with a nearby one whose solution is not.
#
# The period of this orbit is 2 pi sqrt(a^3 / G(m1 + m2)), which for two unit
# masses at a unit semi-major axis is 4.443. The timestep below is that divided
# by two hundred, and the run is two hundred periods.
#
# What to look for in kepler.csv is the relative_energy_error column, and what
# matters about it is its shape rather than its size. Velocity Verlet holds it
# inside an envelope of about 2.7e-3 and stays there: the error at the end of two
# hundred orbits is the error it had after the first few. Run the same file with
#
#     orrery run kepler.orrery --set integrator.kind=rk4 \
#         --set output.diagnostics_path=kepler-rk4.csv
#
# and the column behaves differently. RK4 starts twenty times more accurate, at
# 8.3e-6, and finishes at 1.9e-4, having grown by a factor of twenty-two and
# still growing. It is of higher order and costs four force evaluations a step
# against one, and it is the method whose error has no bound.
#
# So RK4 is the more accurate of the two over this run and the wrong choice for a
# long one, which is the whole of ADR-0011's argument. The two curves cross, and
# where they cross can be watched. With --set run.steps=600000, three thousand
# orbits, velocity Verlet reports 2.685e-3 in the first twentieth of the run and
# 2.689e-3 in the last, unchanged to four digits, while RK4 goes from 1.30e-4 to
# 2.783e-3 and has just overtaken it.

[run]
timestep = 0.02221441469
steps    = 40000
seed     = 1

[initial_conditions]
kind            = kepler
primary_mass    = 1
secondary_mass  = 1
semi_major_axis = 1
eccentricity    = 0.5

[solver]
kind = direct

[integrator]
kind = velocity-verlet

[output]
diagnostics_path   = kepler.csv
diagnostics_stride = 200
